cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use ArduPilot in academic or published work, please cite it as below.
  Please also state the vehicle firmware and version you used (as reported at
  boot and in the logs) or the git commit hash, since results depend on the
  release.
type: software
title: ArduPilot
abstract: >-
  ArduPilot is an open source autopilot system supporting multicopters,
  traditional helicopters, fixed-wing aircraft, VTOL aircraft, rovers, boats,
  submarines, blimps and antenna trackers. It runs on a wide range of
  flight controller hardware and on Linux, and includes software-in-the-loop
  simulation (SITL) for development and testing.
authors:
  - name: ArduPilot Development Team
    website: https://ardupilot.org/dev/docs/common-team.html
  - name: ArduPilot Contributors
repository-code: https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot
url: https://ardupilot.org
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - autopilot
  - unmanned aerial vehicle
  - UAV
  - drone
  - robotics
  - flight control
  - multicopter
  - fixed-wing
  - rover
  - UGV
  - underwater vehicle
  - ROV
  - USV
  - MAVLink
  - SITL
